
Honor keychain distrust at verify time (the distrust veto of the
keychain-union trust model). Anchor exclusion alone rejects a distrusted root,
but not a distrusted intermediate that the server supplies and that also chains
to a legitimately-trusted root, since Go's CertPool has no denylist. This drops
any built chain containing a keychain-distrusted cert. keychainUnionDistrusted lives in
the no-build-tag union file and is populated only on darwin, lazily, when
loadSystemRoots (root_darwin.go) builds the union through
keychainUnionLoadSystemRoots (root_keychainunion_darwin.go) the first time the
system roots are needed; it is nil on every other platform, and this check is
inert there.

The veto applies regardless of VerifyOptions.KeyUsages. The distrust set comes
from the keychain's SSL-policy results, so a certificate marked Never Trust for
SSL also vetoes a chain verified for client auth, S/MIME or any other usage.

